	README.md:  (type=file)
		# cli-test
		
		A new project
		
		## Installation
		
		```sh
		brew tap hay-kot/scaffold-rust-cli-tap
		brew install cli-test
		```
		
		Download a binary from the [releases page](https://github.com/username/cli-test/releases), or build from source:
		
		```sh
		cargo install --locked --git https://github.com/username/cli-test
		```
		
		## Usage
		
		```sh
		cli-test --help
		cli-test hello
		cli-test say-goodbye
		```
		
		Shell completions:
		
		```sh
		cli-test completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_cli-test
		```
		
		## Development
		
		Tools come from [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev), and Rust comes from [rustup](https://rustup.rs) at the version in `rust-toolchain.toml`.
		
		```sh
		mise install       # install the dev tools
		mise run check     # everything CI runs
		mise tasks         # list all tasks
		```
		
		`mise run check` runs these checks, and CI runs the same task:
		
		| Task | Tool | What it checks |
		|---|---|---|
		| `fmt:check` | rustfmt | Formatting, per `rustfmt.toml` |
		| `lint` | clippy | Lints from `[lints]` in `Cargo.toml`, with warnings as errors |
		| `test` | cargo test | Unit tests in `src/` and CLI tests in `tests/` |
		| `docs` | rustdoc | Doc comments build without warnings |
		| `deny` | [cargo-deny](https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-deny) | Security advisories, licenses and crate sources, per `deny.toml` |
		| `tidy` | [cargo-shear](https://github.com/Boshen/cargo-shear) | Dependencies in `Cargo.toml` that the code never uses |
		| `typos` | [typos](https://github.com/crate-ci/typos) | Spelling |
		
		`mise run coverage` writes an `lcov.info` coverage report with [cargo-llvm-cov](https://github.com/taiki-e/cargo-llvm-cov).
		
		### Tests
		
		- Unit tests live next to the code in `#[cfg(test)]` modules. Commands write to a `&mut impl Write`, so a test passes a `Vec<u8>` and checks what was written.
		- CLI tests in `tests/cli.rs` run the built binary with [assert_cmd](https://docs.rs/assert_cmd).
		- [insta](https://insta.rs) is included so snapshot tests are easy to add later. Today it backs only the small inline snapshots in the command tests. It earns its place on large outputs such as help text, JSON, or rendered files. When output changes on purpose, run `cargo insta review` to accept the new snapshot instead of editing the expected text by hand.
		
		### Dependencies
		
		[Renovate](https://docs.renovatebot.com) keeps dependencies current (install the Renovate GitHub app on the repository to turn it on). `renovate.json` sets these rules:
		
		- Crates: `Cargo.toml` names only major versions, so minor and patch updates change only `Cargo.lock`. One weekly PR groups them, and a weekly lockfile refresh picks up transitive updates.
		- The Rust toolchain in `rust-toolchain.toml`, the dev tools in `mise.toml`, and GitHub Actions each get grouped non-major PRs.
		- GitHub Actions are pinned to commit SHAs with the release tag as a comment.
		- Updates wait 7 days after a release. Security fixes from OSV advisories (which include RustSec) skip the wait and the schedule.
		
		### Adding a command
		
		```sh
		scaffold new command
		```
		
		This generates `src/commands/<name>.rs` and registers the command in `src/cli.rs`, `src/commands.rs` and `src/main.rs`.
		
		### Releases
		
		Run the **Build and Publish** workflow from the Actions tab and pick a semver bump. It tags the release and runs GoReleaser, which cross-compiles with [cargo-zigbuild](https://github.com/rust-cross/cargo-zigbuild). Releases build on Linux. The macOS binaries link against zig's bundled macOS stubs, which covers pure-Rust code; a dependency that links Apple frameworks needs a macOS SDK (set `SDKROOT`).
		
		`mise run build` builds a release binary for this machine into `dist/`.
		
	_typos.toml:  (type=file)
		[files]
		extend-exclude = ["target", "dist"]
		
	clippy.toml:  (type=file)
		# Tests may unwrap, panic, index and print: a failing test should fail loudly.
		allow-dbg-in-tests = false
		allow-expect-in-tests = true
		allow-indexing-slicing-in-tests = true
		allow-panic-in-tests = true
		allow-print-in-tests = true
		allow-unwrap-in-tests = true
		
		avoid-breaking-exported-api = false
		cognitive-complexity-threshold = 15
		too-many-arguments-threshold = 5
		too-many-lines-threshold = 80
		
		disallowed-methods = [
		  { path = "std::process::exit", reason = "return an ExitCode from main so destructors run" },
		  { path = "std::env::set_var", reason = "process-wide mutation; pass configuration explicitly" },
		  { path = "std::env::remove_var", reason = "process-wide mutation; pass configuration explicitly" },
		]
		
	deny.toml:  (type=file)
		# cargo-deny checks dependencies for security advisories, licenses, banned
		# crates and unknown sources. Run with `mise run deny`.
		
		[graph]
		all-features = true
		
		[advisories]
		version = 2
		yanked = "deny"
		
		[licenses]
		version = 2
		confidence-threshold = 0.9
		allow = [
		  "Apache-2.0",
		  "Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception",
		  "BSD-2-Clause",
		  "BSD-3-Clause",
		  "ISC",
		  "MIT",
		  "Unicode-3.0",
		  "Zlib",
		]
		
		# This crate sets `publish = false`, so its own license is not checked here.
		[licenses.private]
		ignore = true
		
		[bans]
		multiple-versions = "warn"
		wildcards = "deny"
		allow-wildcard-paths = true
		
		[sources]
		unknown-registry = "deny"
		unknown-git = "deny"
		allow-registry = ["https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"]
		
	mise.toml:  (type=file)
		# Rust itself comes from rustup, pinned by rust-toolchain.toml. Renovate
		# updates these pins.
		[tools]
		cargo-deny = "0.22.0"
		cargo-insta = "1.49.0"
		"github:Boshen/cargo-shear" = "1.14.1"
		"github:rust-cross/cargo-zigbuild" = "0.24.1"
		"github:taiki-e/cargo-llvm-cov" = "0.9.2"
		goreleaser = "2.20.3"
		typos = "1.52.2"
		zig = "0.17.1"
		
		[env]
		LOG_LEVEL = "debug"
		
		[tasks.run]
		description = "Run the main application"
		run = "cargo run --"
		
		[tasks.build]
		description = "Build a release binary for this machine with goreleaser"
		run = "goreleaser build --snapshot --clean --single-target"
		
		[tasks.test]
		description = "Run all tests"
		run = "cargo test --locked"
		
		[tasks.coverage]
		description = "Run tests with coverage and write lcov.info"
		run = "cargo llvm-cov --locked --lcov --output-path lcov.info"
		
		[tasks.fmt]
		description = "Format code"
		run = "cargo fmt --all"
		
		[tasks."fmt:check"]
		description = "Check formatting"
		run = "cargo fmt --all --check"
		
		[tasks.lint]
		description = "Run clippy with warnings as errors"
		run = "cargo clippy --locked --all-targets -- -D warnings"
		
		[tasks.docs]
		description = "Build docs with warnings as errors"
		run = "cargo doc --locked --no-deps --document-private-items"
		env = { RUSTDOCFLAGS = "-D warnings" }
		
		[tasks.deny]
		description = "Check dependencies for advisories, licenses and sources"
		run = "cargo deny --locked check"
		
		[tasks.tidy]
		description = "Find unused dependencies"
		run = "cargo shear"
		
		[tasks.typos]
		description = "Check spelling"
		run = "typos"
		
		[tasks.check]
		description = "Run all checks for PRs (fmt, lint, test, docs, deny, tidy, typos)"
		run = [
		    { task = "fmt:check" },
		    { task = "lint" },
		    { task = "test" },
		    { task = "docs" },
		    { task = "deny" },
		    { task = "tidy" },
		    { task = "typos" },
		]
		
	renovate.json:  (type=file)
		{
		  "$schema": "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
		  "extends": ["config:recommended", "helpers:pinGitHubActionDigestsToSemver"],
		  "labels": ["dependencies"],
		  "schedule": ["before 6am on monday"],
		  "minimumReleaseAge": "7 days",
		  "internalChecksFilter": "strict",
		  "osvVulnerabilityAlerts": true,
		  "vulnerabilityAlerts": {
		    "labels": ["security"],
		    "minimumReleaseAge": null,
		    "schedule": ["at any time"]
		  },
		  "lockFileMaintenance": {
		    "enabled": true,
		    "schedule": ["before 6am on monday"]
		  },
		  "packageRules": [
		    {
		      "description": "Cargo.toml names only the major version, so in-range updates change only Cargo.lock.",
		      "matchManagers": ["cargo"],
		      "rangeStrategy": "update-lockfile"
		    },
		    {
		      "description": "One PR for all non-major crate updates.",
		      "matchManagers": ["cargo"],
		      "matchUpdateTypes": ["minor", "patch"],
		      "groupName": "rust crates (non-major)"
		    },
		    {
		      "description": "One PR for all non-major GitHub Action and digest updates.",
		      "matchManagers": ["github-actions"],
		      "matchUpdateTypes": ["minor", "patch", "digest", "pinDigest"],
		      "groupName": "github actions (non-major)"
		    },
		    {
		      "description": "One PR for all non-major dev tool updates in mise.toml.",
		      "matchManagers": ["mise"],
		      "matchUpdateTypes": ["minor", "patch"],
		      "groupName": "dev tools (non-major)"
		    }
		  ]
		}
		
	rust-toolchain.toml:  (type=file)
		[toolchain]
		channel = "1.100"
		components = ["clippy", "rustfmt", "llvm-tools"]
		profile = "minimal"
		
	rustfmt.toml:  (type=file)
		edition = "2024"
		style_edition = "2024"
		max_width = 100
		newline_style = "Unix"
		use_small_heuristics = "Max"
		use_field_init_shorthand = true
		use_try_shorthand = true
		
	src:  (type=dir)
		build_info.rs:  (type=file)
			//! Build metadata. The release build sets the `BUILD_*` variables at compile
			//! time; local builds fall back to the crate version.
			
			/// The release version, e.g. `1.2.3`.
			pub(crate) const VERSION: &str = match option_env!("BUILD_VERSION") {
			    Some(version) => version,
			    None => env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION"),
			};
			
			const COMMIT: &str = match option_env!("BUILD_COMMIT") {
			    Some(commit) => commit,
			    None => "HEAD",
			};
			
			const DATE: &str = match option_env!("BUILD_DATE") {
			    Some(date) => date,
			    None => "now",
			};
			
			/// The `--version` text: version, short commit and build date.
			pub(crate) fn long_version() -> String {
			    let short_commit = COMMIT.get(..7).unwrap_or(COMMIT);
			    format!("{VERSION} ({short_commit}) {DATE}")
			}
			
			#[cfg(test)]
			mod tests {
			    use super::*;
			
			    #[test]
			    fn long_version_starts_with_version() {
			        assert!(
			            long_version().starts_with(VERSION),
			            "long version should lead with the release version"
			        );
			    }
			}
			
		cli.rs:  (type=file)
			//! Command-line interface definition.
			
			use clap::{Args, Parser, Subcommand, ValueEnum};
			use tracing_subscriber::filter::LevelFilter;
			
			use crate::{build_info, commands};
			
			#[derive(Debug, Parser)]
			#[command(name = "cli-test", version = build_info::VERSION, about, long_about = None)]
			pub(crate) struct Cli {
			    #[command(flatten)]
			    pub(crate) global: GlobalArgs,
			
			    #[command(subcommand)]
			    pub(crate) command: Command,
			}
			
			/// Flags shared by every command.
			#[derive(Debug, Args)]
			pub(crate) struct GlobalArgs {
			    /// Log level
			    #[arg(long, env = "LOG_LEVEL", value_enum, global = true)]
			    pub(crate) log_level: Option<LogLevel>,
			
			    /// Disable colored output
			    #[arg(long, env = "NO_COLOR", global = true)]
			    pub(crate) no_color: bool,
			}
			
			#[derive(Debug, Subcommand)]
			pub(crate) enum Command {
			    /// Run the hello command
			    Hello(commands::hello::Args),
			    /// Run the say-goodbye command
			    SayGoodbye(commands::say_goodbye::Args),
			    // +scaffold:command:variant
			    /// Print a shell completion script
			    Completions(commands::completions::Args),
			}
			#[derive(Debug, Default, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, ValueEnum)]
			pub(crate) enum LogLevel {
			    Trace,
			    Debug,
			    #[default]
			    Info,
			    Warn,
			    Error,
			}
			
			impl From<LogLevel> for LevelFilter {
			    fn from(level: LogLevel) -> Self {
			        match level {
			            LogLevel::Trace => Self::TRACE,
			            LogLevel::Debug => Self::DEBUG,
			            LogLevel::Info => Self::INFO,
			            LogLevel::Warn => Self::WARN,
			            LogLevel::Error => Self::ERROR,
			        }
			    }
			}
			
			#[cfg(test)]
			mod tests {
			    use clap::CommandFactory as _;
			
			    use super::*;
			
			    #[test]
			    fn cli_definition_is_valid() {
			        Cli::command().debug_assert();
			    }
			}
			
		commands:  (type=dir)
			completions.rs:  (type=file)
				//! The `completions` command.
				
				use std::io::Write;
				
				use clap::CommandFactory as _;
				use clap_complete::Shell;
				
				use crate::cli::Cli;
				
				#[derive(Debug, clap::Args)]
				pub(crate) struct Args {
				    /// Shell to generate completions for
				    shell: Shell,
				}
				
				pub(crate) fn run(args: &Args, out: &mut impl Write) {
				    let mut command = Cli::command();
				    let name = command.get_name().to_owned();
				    clap_complete::generate(args.shell, &mut command, name, out);
				}
				
			hello.rs:  (type=file)
				//! The `hello` command.
				
				use std::io::Write;
				
				use super::Context;
				
				#[derive(Debug, clap::Args)]
				pub(crate) struct Args;
				
				pub(crate) fn run(_args: &Args, _ctx: &Context, out: &mut impl Write) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
				    tracing::info!("running hello command");
				
				    writeln!(out, "Hello World!")?;
				    Ok(())
				}
				
				#[cfg(test)]
				mod tests {
				    use super::*;
				
				    #[test]
				    fn prints_greeting() {
				        let mut out = Vec::new();
				        run(&Args, &Context::default(), &mut out).unwrap();
				        insta::assert_snapshot!(String::from_utf8(out).unwrap(), @"Hello World!");
				    }
				}
				
			say_goodbye.rs:  (type=file)
				//! The `say-goodbye` command.
				
				use std::io::Write;
				
				use super::Context;
				
				#[derive(Debug, clap::Args)]
				pub(crate) struct Args;
				
				pub(crate) fn run(_args: &Args, _ctx: &Context, out: &mut impl Write) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
				    tracing::info!("running say-goodbye command");
				
				    writeln!(out, "Hello World!")?;
				    Ok(())
				}
				
				#[cfg(test)]
				mod tests {
				    use super::*;
				
				    #[test]
				    fn prints_greeting() {
				        let mut out = Vec::new();
				        run(&Args, &Context::default(), &mut out).unwrap();
				        insta::assert_snapshot!(String::from_utf8(out).unwrap(), @"Hello World!");
				    }
				}
				
		commands.rs:  (type=file)
			//! Subcommand implementations. Each command writes its output to the writer
			//! it is given, so tests can capture it.
			
			pub(crate) mod completions;
			pub(crate) mod hello;
			pub(crate) mod say_goodbye;
			// +scaffold:command:module
			
			/// Settings that shape how every command writes output.
			#[derive(Debug, Default)]
			#[expect(
			    clippy::empty_structs_with_brackets,
			    reason = "commands build it with `Context::default()`, which keeps working once fields exist"
			)]
			pub(crate) struct Context {}
			
		logging.rs:  (type=file)
			//! Tracing setup. Logs go to stderr so stdout stays free for command output.
			
			use anyhow::Context as _;
			use tracing_subscriber::filter::LevelFilter;
			use tracing_subscriber::fmt;
			use tracing_subscriber::prelude::*;
			
			use crate::cli::LogLevel;
			
			/// Installs the global subscriber, logging to stderr.
			pub(crate) fn init(level: LogLevel, color: bool) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
			    tracing_subscriber::registry()
			        .with(LevelFilter::from(level))
			        .with(fmt::layer().with_writer(std::io::stderr).with_ansi(color))
			        .try_init()
			        .context("installing the tracing subscriber")
			}
			
		main.rs:  (type=file)
			//! A new project
			
			mod build_info;
			mod cli;
			mod commands;
			mod logging;
			
			use std::io::{self, IsTerminal as _};
			use std::process::ExitCode;
			
			use clap::{CommandFactory as _, FromArgMatches as _};
			
			use crate::cli::{Cli, Command};
			
			fn main() -> ExitCode {
			    let matches = Cli::command().long_version(build_info::long_version()).get_matches();
			    let cli = match Cli::from_arg_matches(&matches) {
			        Ok(cli) => cli,
			        Err(err) => err.exit(),
			    };
			
			    let color = !cli.global.no_color && io::stderr().is_terminal();
			    match run(cli) {
			        Ok(()) => ExitCode::SUCCESS,
			        Err(err) => {
			            report(&err, color);
			            ExitCode::FAILURE
			        }
			    }
			}
			
			fn run(cli: Cli) -> anyhow::Result<()> {
			    let log_level = cli.global.log_level.unwrap_or_default();
			    logging::init(log_level, !cli.global.no_color)?;
			    let ctx = commands::Context::default();
			    let mut out = io::stdout().lock();
			
			    match cli.command {
			        Command::Hello(args) => commands::hello::run(&args, &ctx, &mut out),
			        Command::SayGoodbye(args) => commands::say_goodbye::run(&args, &ctx, &mut out),
			        // +scaffold:command:dispatch
			        Command::Completions(args) => {
			            commands::completions::run(&args, &mut out);
			            Ok(())
			        }
			    }
			}
			
			/// Writes `err` and its causes to stderr as `error: <message>: <cause>`.
			fn report(err: &anyhow::Error, color: bool) {
			    // Nothing useful remains to do if stderr itself is gone.
			    let _ignored = write_report(&mut io::stderr().lock(), err, color);
			}
			
			fn write_report(out: &mut impl io::Write, err: &anyhow::Error, color: bool) -> io::Result<()> {
			    let (red, reset) = if color { ("\x1b[1;31m", "\x1b[0m") } else { ("", "") };
			    writeln!(out, "{red}error:{reset} {err:#}")
			}
			
			#[cfg(test)]
			mod tests {
			    use super::*;
			
			    #[test]
			    fn report_prints_the_error_and_its_causes() {
			        let err = anyhow::anyhow!("file not found").context("loading config");
			        let mut out = Vec::new();
			        write_report(&mut out, &err, false).unwrap();
			        insta::assert_snapshot!(
			            String::from_utf8(out).unwrap(),
			            @"error: loading config: file not found"
			        );
			    }
			}
			
	tests:  (type=dir)
		cli.rs:  (type=file)
			//! End-to-end tests that run the compiled binary.
			
			#[cfg(test)]
			mod cli {
			    use assert_cmd::Command;
			    use predicates::str::contains;
			
			    fn bin() -> Command {
			        Command::cargo_bin(env!("CARGO_PKG_NAME")).unwrap()
			    }
			
			    #[test]
			    fn help_lists_commands() {
			        bin()
			            .arg("--help")
			            .assert()
			            .success()
			            .stdout(contains("hello"))
			            .stdout(contains("say-goodbye"))
			            .stdout(contains("completions"));
			    }
			
			    #[test]
			    fn version_prints_crate_version() {
			        bin().arg("--version").assert().success().stdout(contains(env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")));
			    }
			
			    #[test]
			    fn hello_prints_greeting() {
			        bin().args(["--no-color", "hello"]).assert().success().stdout("Hello World!\n");
			    }
			
			    #[test]
			    fn say_goodbye_prints_greeting() {
			        bin().args(["--no-color", "say-goodbye"]).assert().success().stdout("Hello World!\n");
			    }
			
			    #[test]
			    fn unknown_command_fails() {
			        bin().arg("not-a-command").assert().failure();
			    }
			
			    #[test]
			    fn completions_generates_a_script() {
			        bin().args(["completions", "bash"]).assert().success().stdout(contains("cli-test"));
			    }
			}
			

